//   - side: Indicates if matrix Ai is on the left or right of Xi
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix Ai lower or upper part is stored, the other part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - trans: Operation op( Ai) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - diag: Indicates if the elements on the main diagonal of matrix Ai are unity and should not be accessed
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix Bi, with matrix Ai sized accordingly
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix Bi, with matrix Ai is sized accordingly
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication, if alpha == 0 then Ai is not referenced and Bi does not have to be a valid input
//   - A: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. lda x m with lda >= max(1, m) if side == [SideLeft] and lda x n with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix Ai
//   - B: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m). Matrices Bi should not overlap; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix Bi
//   - batchCount: Number of pointers contained in A and B
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0, n < 0, or - if trans is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if side is not one of [SideLeft] and [SideRight], or - if diag is not one of [DiagUnit] and [DiagNonUnit], or - if lda < max(1, m) if side == [SideLeft], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m)
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasCtrsmBatched.
