// Dasum This function computes the sum of the absolute values of the elements of vector x.
//
// Hence, the result is ∑i=1n|Im(xj)|+|Re(xj)| where j=1+(i−1)∗incx . Notice that the last equation reflects 1-based indexing used for compatibility with Fortran. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: sasum(), dasum(), scasum(), dzasum()
