// Dgeam This function performs the matrix-matrix addition/transposition C=αop(A)+βop(B) where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(A)m×n , op(B)m×n and Cm×n , respectively.
//
// Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(B) is defined similarly for matrix B . The operation is out-of-place if C does not overlap A or B. The in-place mode supports the following two operations, C=α*C+βop(B) C=αop(A)+β*C For in-place mode, if C == A, ldc == lda and transa == [OpN]. If C === B, ldc == ldb and transb == [OpN]. If the user does not meet above requirements, [ErrInvalidValue] is returned. The operation includes the following special cases: the user can reset matrix C to zero by setting *alpha = beta = 0. the user can transpose matrix A by setting *alpha = 1 and *beta = 0. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( B) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( A) and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( B) and C
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *alpha == 0, A does not have to be a valid input
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x n with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *beta == 0, B does not have to be a valid input
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x m with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0, or - if transa is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if transb is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m) if transb == [OpN], and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if A == C and `(transa != [OpN])
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasDgeam.
func (h Handle) Dgeam(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int32, n int32, alpha *float64, A *float64, lda int32, beta *float64, B *float64, ldb int32, C *float64, ldc int32) error {
	return dgeam(h, transa, transb, m, n, alpha, A, lda, beta, B, ldb, C, ldc)
}

// Dgeam64 This function performs the matrix-matrix addition/transposition C=αop(A)+βop(B) where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(A)m×n , op(B)m×n and Cm×n , respectively.
//
// Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(B) is defined similarly for matrix B . The operation is out-of-place if C does not overlap A or B. The in-place mode supports the following two operations, C=α*C+βop(B) C=αop(A)+β*C For in-place mode, if C == A, ldc == lda and transa == [OpN]. If C === B, ldc == ldb and transb == [OpN]. If the user does not meet above requirements, [ErrInvalidValue] is returned. The operation includes the following special cases: the user can reset matrix C to zero by setting *alpha = beta = 0. the user can transpose matrix A by setting *alpha = 1 and *beta = 0. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( B) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( A) and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( B) and C
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *alpha == 0, A does not have to be a valid input
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x n with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If *beta == 0, B does not have to be a valid input
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x m with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0, or - if transa is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if transb is not one of [OpN], [OpT] and [OpC], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m) if transb == [OpN], and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if A == C and `(transa != [OpN])
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasDgeam_64.
func (h Handle) Dgeam64(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int64, n int64, alpha *float64, A *float64, lda int64, beta *float64, B *float64, ldb int64, C *float64, ldc int64) error {
	return dgeam64(h, transa, transb, m, n, alpha, A, lda, beta, B, ldb, C, ldc)
}

// DgelsBatched Aarray is an array of pointers to matrices stored in column-major format.
//
// This function find the least squares solution of a batch of overdetermined systems: it solves the least squares problem described as follows : On exit, each Aarrayi is overwritten with their QR factorization and each Carrayi is overwritten with the least square solution cublasgelsBatched supports only the non-transpose operation and only solves over-determined systems (m >= n). cublasgelsBatched only supports compute capability 2.0 or above. This function is intended to be used for matrices of small sizes where the launch overhead is a significant factor. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: sgels(), dgels(), cgels(), zgels()
//
//   - trans: Operation op( Aarrayi) that is non- or (conj.) transpose. Only non-transpose operation is currently supported
//   - m: Number of rows of each Aarrayi and Carrayi if trans == [OpN], numbers of columns of each Aarrayi otherwise (not supported currently)
//   - n: Number of columns of each Aarrayi if trans == [OpN], and number of rows of each Aarrayi and Carrayi otherwise (not supported currently)
//   - nrhs: Number of columns of each Carrayi
//   - Aarray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. m x n with lda >= max(1, m) if trans == [OpN], and n x m with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise (not supported currently). Matrices Aarrayi should not overlap; otherwise, behavior is undefined
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Aarrayi
//   - Carray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. m x nrhs with ldc >= max(1, m) if trans == [OpN], and n x nrhs with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise (not supported currently). Matrices Carrayi should not overlap; otherwise, behavior is undefined
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Carrayi
//   - info: If info == 0 the parameters passed to the function are validIf info < 0 the parameter in position -info is invalid
//   - devInfoArray: Optional array of integers of dimension batchsize.If non-null, every element of devInfoArrayi == V has the following meaning:V == 0 : the i-th problem was successfully solvedV > 0 : the V-th diagonal element of the Aarrayi is zero. Aarrayi does not have full rank
//   - batchSize: Number of pointers contained in Aarray and Carray
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0 or nrhs < 0 or batchSize < 0 or - if lda < max(1, m) or ldc < max(1, m)
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusNotSupported: The parameters m <n or trans is different from non-transpose.
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasDgelsBatched.
func (h Handle) DgelsBatched(trans Operation, m int32, n int32, nrhs int32, Aarray uintptr, lda int32, Carray uintptr, ldc int32, info *int32, devInfoArray *int32, batchSize int32) error {
	return dgelsBatched(h, trans, m, n, nrhs, Aarray, lda, Carray, ldc, info, devInfoArray, batchSize)
}

// DgemmBatched This function performs the matrix-matrix multiplication of a batch of matrices.
//
// The batch is considered to be “uniform”, i.e. all instances have the same dimensions (m, n, k), leading dimensions (lda, ldb, ldc) and transpositions (transa, transb) for their respective A, B and C matrices. The address of the input matrices and the output matrix of each instance of the batch are read from arrays of pointers passed to the function by the caller. Ci=αop(Ai)op(Bi)+βCi, for i ∈[0,batchCount−1] where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are arrays of pointers to matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(Ai)m×k , op(Bi)k×n and Cim×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(Bi) is defined similarly for matrix Bi . Note Ci matrices must not overlap, that is, the individual gemm operations must be computable independently; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected. On certain problem sizes, it might be advantageous to make multiple calls to cublasgemm() in different CUDA streams, rather than use this API. If math mode enables fast math modes when using [Handle.SgemmBatched], pointers (not the pointer arrays) placed in the GPU memory must be properly aligned to avoid misaligned memory access errors. Ideally all pointers are aligned to at least 16 Bytes. Otherwise it is recommended that they meet the following rule: The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( Ai) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( Bi) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( Ai) and Ci
//   - n: Number of columns of op( Bi) and Ci
//   - k: Number of columns of op( Ai) and rows of op( Bi)
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - Aarray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. lda x k with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Ai
//   - Barray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, k) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x k with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Bi
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, C does not have to be a valid input
//   - Carray: Array of pointers to < type > array. It has dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m). Matrices Ci should not overlap; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Ci
//   - batchCount: Number of pointers contained in Aarray, Barray and Carray
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusArchMismatch: [Handle.HgemmBatched] is only supported for GPU with architecture capabilities equal or greater than 5.3
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0 or k < 0, or - if transa and transb are not one of [OpN], [OpC], [OpT], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN] and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, k) when transb == [OpN] and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m)
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasDgemmBatched.
func (h Handle) DgemmBatched(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int32, n int32, k int32, alpha *float64, Aarray uintptr, lda int32, Barray uintptr, ldb int32, beta *float64, Carray uintptr, ldc int32, batchCount int32) error {
	return dgemmBatched(h, transa, transb, m, n, k, alpha, Aarray, lda, Barray, ldb, beta, Carray, ldc, batchCount)
}

// DgemmBatched64 This function performs the matrix-matrix multiplication of a batch of matrices.
//
// The batch is considered to be “uniform”, i.e. all instances have the same dimensions (m, n, k), leading dimensions (lda, ldb, ldc) and transpositions (transa, transb) for their respective A, B and C matrices. The address of the input matrices and the output matrix of each instance of the batch are read from arrays of pointers passed to the function by the caller. Ci=αop(Ai)op(Bi)+βCi, for i ∈[0,batchCount−1] where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are arrays of pointers to matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(Ai)m×k , op(Bi)k×n and Cim×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(Bi) is defined similarly for matrix Bi . Note Ci matrices must not overlap, that is, the individual gemm operations must be computable independently; otherwise, undefined behavior is expected. On certain problem sizes, it might be advantageous to make multiple calls to cublasgemm() in different CUDA streams, rather than use this API. If math mode enables fast math modes when using [Handle.SgemmBatched], pointers (not the pointer arrays) placed in the GPU memory must be properly aligned to avoid misaligned memory access errors. Ideally all pointers are aligned to at least 16 Bytes. Otherwise it is recommended that they meet the following rule: The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( Ai) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( Bi) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( Ai) and Ci
//   - n: Number of columns of op( Bi) and Ci
//   - k: Number of columns of op( Ai) and rows of op( Bi)
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - Aarray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. lda x k with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Ai
//   - Barray: Array of pointers to < type > array, with each array of dim. ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, k) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x k with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Bi
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, C does not have to be a valid input
