// GemmBatchedEx This function is an extension of cublasgemmBatched() that performs the matrix-matrix multiplication of a batch of matrices and allows the user to individually specify the data types for each of the A, B and C matrix arrays, the precision of computation and the GEMM algorithm to be run.
//
// Like cublasgemmBatched(), the batch is considered to be “uniform”, i.e. all instances have the same dimensions (m, n, k), leading dimensions (lda, ldb, ldc) and transpositions (transa, transb) for their respective A, B and C matrices. The address of the input matrices and the output matrix of each instance of the batch are read from arrays of pointers passed to the function by the caller. Supported combinations of arguments are listed further down in this section. Note The second variant of [Handle.GemmBatchedEx] function is provided for backward compatibility with C++ applications code, where the computeType parameter is of [DataType] instead of [ComputeType]. C applications would still compile with the updated function signature. Ci=αop(Ai)op(Bi)+βCi, for i ∈[0,batchCount−1] where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are arrays of pointers to matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(Ai)m×k , op(Bi)k×n and Cim×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(Bi) is defined similarly for matrix Bi . Note Ci matrices must not overlap, i.e. the individual gemm operations must be computable independently; otherwise, behavior is undefined. On certain problem sizes, it might be advantageous to make multiple calls to cublasgemm() in different CUDA streams, rather than use this API. [Handle.GemmBatchedEx] supports the following Compute Type, Scale Type, Atype/Btype, and Ctype: If Atype is CUDA_R_16F or CUDA_R_16BF, or computeType is any of the FAST options, or when math mode or algo enable fast math modes, pointers (not the pointer arrays) placed in the GPU memory must be properly aligned to avoid misaligned memory access errors. Ideally all pointers are aligned to at least 16 Bytes. Otherwise it is recommended that they meet the following rule: Note Compute types [Compute32I] and [Compute32IPedantic] are only supported with all pointers Ai, Bi being 4-byte aligned and lda, ldb being multiples of 4. For a better performance, it is also recommended that IMMA kernels requirements for the regular data ordering listed here are met. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. Also refer to: sgemm.()
//
//   - transa: Operation op( Aarrayi) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( Barrayi) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( Aarrayi) and Carrayi
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( Barrayi) and Carrayi
//   - k: Number of columns of op( Aarrayi) and rows of op( Barrayi)
//   - alpha: Scaling factor for matrix products of the type that corresponds to the computeType and Ctype, see the table below for details
//   - Aarray: Array of pointers to < Atype > array, with each array of dim. lda x k with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - Atype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of Aarray
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix Aarrayi
//   - Barray: Array of pointers to < Btype > array, with each array of dim. ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, k) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x k with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - Btype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of Barray
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix Barrayi
//   - beta: Scaling factor for Carray of the type that corresponds to the computeType and Ctype, see the table below for details. If beta == 0, Carrayi does not have to be a valid input
//   - Carray: Array of pointers to < Ctype > array. It has dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m). Matrices Carrayi should not overlap; otherwise, the behavior is undefined.All pointers must meet certain alignment criteria. Please see below for details
//   - Ctype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of Carray
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store each matrix Carrayi
//   - batchCount: Number of pointers contained in Aarray, Barray and Carray
//   - computeType: Enumerant specifying the computation type
//   - algo: Enumerant specifying the algorithm. See [GemmAlgo]
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusArchMismatch: [Handle.GemmBatchedEx] is only supported for GPU with architecture capabilities equal to or greater than 5.0.
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU.
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0 or k < 0, or - if transa and transb are not one of [OpN], [OpC], [OpT], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN] and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, k) when transb == [OpN] and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if Atype or Btype or Ctype or algo or computeType is not supported
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized.
//   - StatusNotSupported: The combination of the parameters Atype, Btype and Ctype or the algorithm, algo is not supported.
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully.
//
// Wraps cublasGemmBatchedEx.
func (h Handle) GemmBatchedEx(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int32, n int32, k int32, alpha uintptr, Aarray uintptr, Atype DataType, lda int32, Barray uintptr, Btype DataType, ldb int32, beta uintptr, Carray uintptr, Ctype DataType, ldc int32, batchCount int32, computeType ComputeType, algo GemmAlgo) error {
	return gemmBatchedEx(h, transa, transb, m, n, k, alpha, Aarray, Atype, lda, Barray, Btype, ldb, beta, Carray, Ctype, ldc, batchCount, computeType, algo)
}

