// GemmEx This function is an extension of cublasgemm() that allows the user to individually specify the data types for each of the A, B and C matrices, the precision of computation and the GEMM algorithm to be run.
//
// Supported combinations of arguments are listed further down in this section. Note The second variant of [Handle.GemmEx] function is provided for backward compatibility with C++ applications code, where the computeType parameter is of [DataType] instead of [ComputeType]. C applications would still compile with the updated function signature. This function is only supported on devices with compute capability 5.0 or later. C=αop(A)op(B)+βC where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(A)m×k , op(B)k×n and Cm×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(B) is defined similarly for matrix B . [Handle.GemmEx] supports the following Compute Type, Scale Type, Atype/Btype, and Ctype: Note [Compute32I] and [Compute32IPedantic] compute types are only supported with A, B being 4-byte aligned and lda, ldb being multiples of 4. For better performance, it is also recommended that IMMA kernels requirements for a regular data ordering listed here are met. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed in the following table. Starting with release 11.2, using the typed functions instead of the extension functions (cublas**Ex()) helps in reducing the binary size when linking to static cuBLAS Library. Also refer to: sgemm.() For more information about the numerical behavior of some GEMM algorithms, refer to the GEMM Algorithms Numerical Behavior section.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( B) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( A) and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( B) and C
//   - k: Number of columns of op( A) and rows of op( B)
//   - alpha: Scaling factor for A*B of the type that corresponds to the computeType and Ctype, see the table below for details
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x k with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise
//   - Atype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix A
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, k) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x k with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise
//   - Btype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix B
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - beta: Scaling factor for C of the type that corresponds to the computeType and Ctype, see the table below for details. If beta == 0, C does not have to be a valid input
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - Ctype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix C
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//   - computeType: Enumerant specifying the computation type
//   - algo: Enumerant specifying the algorithm. See [GemmAlgo]
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusArchMismatch: [Handle.GemmEx] is only supported for GPU with architecture capabilities equal or greater than 5.0.
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU.
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0 or k < 0, or - if transa and transb are not one of [OpN], [OpC], [OpT], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN] and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, k) when transb == [OpN] and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if C is NULL when beta is not zero - if Atype or Btype or Ctype or algo are not supported
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized.
//   - StatusNotSupported: The combination of the parameters Atype, Btype and Ctype or the algorithm, algo is not supported.
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully.
//
// Wraps cublasGemmEx.
func (h Handle) GemmEx(transa Operation, transb Operation, m int32, n int32, k int32, alpha uintptr, A uintptr, Atype DataType, lda int32, B uintptr, Btype DataType, ldb int32, beta uintptr, C uintptr, Ctype DataType, ldc int32, computeType ComputeType, algo GemmAlgo) error {
	return gemmEx(h, transa, transb, m, n, k, alpha, A, Atype, lda, B, Btype, ldb, beta, C, Ctype, ldc, computeType, algo)
}

