// Icamax This function finds the (smallest) index of the element of the maximum magnitude.
//
// Hence, the result is the first i such that |Im(xj)|+|Re(xj)| is maximum for i=1,…,n and j=1+(i−1)∗ incx . Notice that the last equation reflects 1-based indexing used for compatibility with Fortran. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: isamax(), idamax(), icamax(), izamax()
//
//   - n: Number of elements in the vector x
//   - x: < type > vector with elements
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusAllocFailed: The reduction buffer could not be allocated
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: result is NULL
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasIcamax_v2.
