// Nrm2Ex This function is an API generalization of the routine cublasnrm2() where input data, output data and compute type can be specified independently.
//
// This function computes the Euclidean norm of the vector x. The code uses a multiphase model of accumulation to avoid intermediate underflow and overflow, with the result being equivalent to ∑i=1n(xj×xj) where j=1+(i−1)∗incx in exact arithmetic. Notice that the last equation reflects 1-based indexing used for compatibility with Fortran. The datatypes combinations currently supported for [Handle.Nrm2Ex] are listed below : The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: snrm2(), dnrm2(), scnrm2(), dznrm2()
