// SgemmEx This function is an extension of cublasgemm().
//
// In this function the input matrices and output matrices can have a lower precision but the computation is still done in the type . For example, in the type float for [Handle.SgemmEx] and in the type [Complex64] for [Handle.CgemmEx]. C=αop(A)op(B)+βC where α and β are scalars, and A , B and C are matrices stored in column-major format with dimensions op(A)m×k , op(B)k×n and Cm×n , respectively. Also, for matrix A op(A)={Aif transa == CUBLAS_OP_NATif transa == CUBLAS_OP_TAHif transa == [OpC] and op(B) is defined similarly for matrix B . The matrix types combinations supported for [Handle.SgemmEx] are listed below: The matrix types combinations supported for [Handle.CgemmEx] are listed below : The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: sgemm() For more information about the numerical behavior of some GEMM algorithms, refer to the GEMM Algorithms Numerical Behavior section.
//
//   - transa: Operation op( A) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - transb: Operation op( B) that is non- or (conj.) transpose
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix op( A) and C
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix op( B) and C
//   - k: Number of columns of op( A) and rows of op( B)
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type > array of dimensions lda x k with lda >= max(1, m) if transa == [OpN] and lda x m with lda >= max(1, k) otherwise
//   - Atype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix A
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store the matrix A
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, k) if transb == [OpN] and ldb x k with ldb >= max(1,n) otherwise
//   - Btype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix B
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0, C does not have to be a valid input
//   - C: < type > array of dimensions ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - Ctype: Enumerant specifying the datatype of matrix C
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of a two-dimensional array used to store the matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusArchMismatch: [Handle.CgemmEx] is only supported for GPU with architecture capabilities equal or greater than 5.0
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0 or k < 0, or - if transa and transb are not one of [OpN], [OpC], [OpT], or - if lda < max(1, m) when transa == [OpN] and lda < max(1, k) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, k) when transb == [OpN] and ldb < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if C is NULL when beta is not zero
