// Sspmv This function performs the symmetric packed matrix-vector multiplication y=αAx+βy where A is a n×n symmetric matrix stored in packed format, x and y are vectors, and α and β are scalars.
//
// If uplo == [FillModeLower] then the elements in the lower triangular part of the symmetric matrix A are packed together column by column without gaps, so that the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location AP [i+((2*n-j+1)*j)/2] for j=1,…,n and i≥j . Consequently, the packed format requires only n(n+1)2 elements for storage. If uplo == [FillModeUpper] then the elements in the upper triangular part of the symmetric matrix A are packed together column by column without gaps, so that the element A(i,j) is stored in the memory location AP [i+(j*(j+1))/2] for j=1,…,n and i≤j . Consequently, the packed format requires only n(n+1)2 elements for storage. The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: sspmv(), dspmv()
//
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other symmetric part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - n: Number of rows and columns of matrix A
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - AP: < type > array with A stored in packed format
//   - x: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incx: Stride between consecutive elements of x
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0 then y does not have to be a valid input
//   - y: < type > vector with n elements
//   - incy: Stride between consecutive elements of y
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If n < 0, or - if incx == 0 or incy == 0, or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if alpha or beta are NULL
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasSspmv_v2.
func (h Handle) Sspmv(uplo FillMode, n int32, alpha *float32, AP *float32, x *float32, incx int32, beta *float32, y *float32, incy int32) error {
	return sspmv(h, uplo, n, alpha, AP, x, incx, beta, y, incy)
}

