// Ssymm This function performs the symmetric matrix-matrix multiplication C={αAB+βCif side == [SideLeft]αBA+βCif side == [SideRight] where A is a symmetric matrix stored in lower or upper mode, B and C are m×n matrices, and α and β are scalars.
//
// The possible error values returned by this function and their meanings are listed below. For references please refer to NETLIB documentation: ssymm(), dsymm(), csymm(), zsymm()
//
//   - side: Indicates if matrix A is on the left or right of B
//   - uplo: Indicates if matrix A lower or upper part is stored, the other symmetric part is not referenced and is inferred from the stored elements
//   - m: Number of rows of matrix C and B, with matrix A sized accordingly
//   - n: Number of columns of matrix C and B, with matrix A sized accordingly
//   - alpha: < type > scalar used for multiplication
//   - A: < type > array of dimension lda x m with lda >= max(1, m) if side == [SideLeft] and lda x n with lda >= max(1, n) otherwise
//   - lda: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix A
//   - B: < type > array of dimension ldb x n with ldb >= max(1, m)
//   - ldb: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix B
//   - beta: < type > scalar used for multiplication. If beta == 0 then C does not have to be a valid input
//   - C: < type > array of dimension ldc x n with ldc >= max(1, m)
//   - ldc: Leading dimension of two-dimensional array used to store matrix C
//
// Returns:
//   - StatusExecutionFailed: The function failed to launch on the GPU
//   - StatusInvalidValue: - If m < 0 or n < 0, or - if side is not one of [SideLeft] and [SideRight], or - if uplo is not one of [FillModeLower] and [FillModeUpper], or - if lda < max(1, m) when side == [SideLeft], and lda < max(1, n) otherwise, or - if ldb < max(1, m), or - if ldc < max(1, m), or - if alpha or beta are NULL, or - if C is NULL when beta is not zero
//   - StatusNotInitialized: The library was not initialized
//   - StatusSuccess: The operation completed successfully
//
// Wraps cublasSsymm_v2.
func (h Handle) Ssymm(side SideMode, uplo FillMode, m int32, n int32, alpha *float32, A *float32, lda int32, B *float32, ldb int32, beta *float32, C *float32, ldc int32) error {
	return ssymm(h, side, uplo, m, n, alpha, A, lda, B, ldb, beta, C, ldc)
}

// Ssymm64 This function performs the symmetric matrix-matrix multiplication C={αAB+βCif side == [SideLeft]αBA+βCif side == [SideRight] where A is a symmetric matrix stored in lower or upper mode, B and C are m×n matrices, and α and β are scalars.
